+# Controller posture integration
+
+Implemented in source (cloud validation pending):
+- Reuse existing keyboard + touchpad mode; clearer combined label and gesture hint.
+- Local/wireless gamepad central touchpad uses existing Link gestures, with separate local pointer ownership from mapped gamepad buttons.
+- Pointer/scroll sensitivity persisted on controller; fractional motion retained without timers.
+- Duo gamepad layout menu: Automatic, Wide, Portrait, Tabletop. Portrait has a large upper touchpad and rearranged full-size controls. Tabletop separates upper touchpad and lower controls around the active horizontal reserved region; manual fallback uses a visible-free 32pt gap. Automatic does not infer hinge angles or activate on iPads.
+- Geometry/layout change releases held gamepad and pointer input; native surface cancels fingers on geometry change.
+- Tests: geometry overlap/bounds, posture selection, fractional motion/normalisation/persistence, source ownership and real production Simulator UI interactions.
+
+Next: compile against actual Xcode SDK, run native + production controller UI tests and inspect screenshots. No IPA requested for this development checkpoint. The USB touchscreen replacement remains a separate integration requirement; current controller touchpad is pointer input and requires no CoreHID entitlement.
+
+## Added scope
+- Optional main-display video mirror, no extra guest monitor. Existing hardware encoder/decoder/TLS path; bounded three-frame credits, unique frame IDs across replacements, one replaceable display image and demand-driven 60/120Hz display pulse.
+- Duo portrait video/controller deck and full-window landscape overlay; Fit/Fill, Video off, Reconnect and refresh controls.
+- Opt-in CoreMotion steering, calibration and angle/inversion; LX only, LY/buttons preserved, existing owned A/D mapping. One foreground motion owner and no idle sensor updates.
+- Listener/key retained on peer socket loss; client has cancellable bounded exponential reconnect and immediate foreground retry. Explicit disconnect stops retries. Background does not keep the VM/controller alive.
+- Audio interruption/route/reset/foreground recovery with generation fencing and bounded retries. Native pause now preserves guest sound-running state; transient start failure can restore its backend. Linux production-backend ASan/UBSan tests pass. Full SDK/VM/real TLS/Metal tests pending.
+
+Cloud checkpoint b0cd93e: pure controller tests passed. Full integration identified missing standalone-fixture hardware symbol and a sanitizer-script Swift source list; both repaired. First Simulator test could not resolve UIKeyInput touchpad as an Other element; now queries the exact identifier across accessibility types. No test skipped. New source must pass both real production UI and full native/app compile before release.
+
+## Entitlement-free touchscreen integration
+- Upstream PR32 USB commit385a4f6 integrated selectively; gamepad port3 preserved, touchscreen port4. Both guest input devices can connect together.
+- Removed CoreHID virtual-device implementation and restricted guest entitlements. Native touch remains experimental for macOS27.2+; unavailable guests fall back to trackpad.
+- Bounded helper stdio/HTTP transport, epoch checks, watchdog, deferred UUID mapping, guest contact lifts and queue isolation retained. Runner companion paths retained.
+- Snapshot fingerprint includes expanded xHCI; restore discards old queued motion and requires fresh touch-helper mapping. Pause fences helper epoch before serialization.
+- Two signed guest app bundles inside deterministic tar.gz, empty entitlements, architecture/signature/archive-path validation in CI and IPA inspector. Guest helper update required.
+- Optional video encoding now has explicit60/120Hz capture budgets and one deferred latest-frame refresh after cadence/credit backpressure. Decoder ACK sequence IDs survive encoder replacement; remote display presents at the selected supported cadence with one latest image.
+- Source4f55 passed all native/sanitizer/SDK/Release app compilation (run43281138121). M4 UI actions reached the final keyboard/gamepad return but exceeded the old180s test allowance; the expanded full-feature suite now has480s. Duo canvas boot timed out externally before app launch; retain run43281138212 evidence and retry exact next source. No ignored failures and no IPA.
+
+## M4 pacing and disk expansion
+- New0.3.4 M4 logsACBA: four vCPUs,14GiB guest RAM, grouped/superblocks enabled;12 LPM diagnostic samples, host presentations14.12..29.60/s (median24.98), Normal thermal category. Not game FPS. Recommend8GiB baseline and experiments off for controlled comparison; do not silently rewrite saved VM RAM.
+- Native CAMetalDisplayLink no longer competes with a commit-relative wall-clock deadline. It remains armed during actual damage, pauses at the first idle pulse, avoids redundant main/presenter preflight while unchanged, and requests the selected supported cadence. Real M4 frame-time improvement remains hardware validation; the old dual gate demonstrably rejects alternate60Hz pulses with2ms commit delay.
+- Offline disk growth: presets128/256/512GiB and custom to2048GiB. Native validated GPT CRC/backup relocation, clone+atomic replacement and original image backup. VM/file locks, no shrink/live/saved-session mutation. APFS is extended using macOS diskutil after next cold boot; recovery partitions are never moved speculatively. Linux production-GPT tests passed ASan/UBSan with independent Python CRC oracle. Cloud macOS tests use the actual filesystem clone API.
+- Cloud3ee78 failed before compilation because changing the reconciliation script's pre-patch helper token changed the patch baseline. Fixed by preserving the reviewed baseline token; cumulative patch itself owns the new tar.gz build phase. Retest next exact source, no waived failure/no IPA.
+
+- Bounded diagnostic capture now activates the existing presented-time histogram, including p95/p99, without a new sampler/timer. Capture epochs fence late presented callbacks; explicit HV_FRAME_STATS remains respected. Histograms include idle/cursor intervals and are not game FPS.
+- Audio CPU-only background continuation resets the fallback stream clock while keeping the guest's playing state. Touch helper watchdog runs only while a USB touchscreen device is active, rather than waking when disabled.
+
+Cloud4a5966 exposed Darwin feature visibility in disk_resize.c: POSIX-only declarations hid O_NOFOLLOW/flock; use Darwin feature set on Apple, POSIX elsewhere. Disk GPT regression and audio lifecycle pass locally. Stats lifecycle failure was missing test_vm_lifecycle binary after that compile error, not a waived assertion.
+Hardware codec fixture now models the production serial GPU worker's requestFrame callback. It verifies paced retry, three-credit blocked-consumer ceiling and final deferred snapshot after ACK (37 actual decoded frames), instead of expecting unpaced burst captures. Full macOS run required before release.
+
+Cloud91f832 passes native JIT/MMU/memory/device and lifecycle/sanitizer suites, including actual37-frame codec/TLS tests at all three canvas sizes and production display pulse fixture. The full SDK check found NativeTouchSurface's upstream Trackpad.revealTap name does not exist in the fork; route its four-finger menu gesture to the existing Trackpad.threeFingerTap notification (one existing SessionView consumer). No duplicated menu path.
+
+Cloud83dbcf passes all88 production Swift sources against iPhoneOS27.2 plus JIT/MMU/device/lifecycle/sanitizers. USB's disabled-touch SupportedProtocol fixture still expected upstream two ports; the fork correctly advertises keyboard/trackpad/gamepad(three). Corrected that test expectation; complete actual xHCI USB transfers/lifts/overflow/reset/hotplug/watchdog/coexistence pass locally under ASan/UBSan with explicit Linux-only RAM/PCI/CPU-wake boundaries (not a native machine pass). Native cloud test still uses the real machine/PCI. Helper validation now collects independent compile/package/SDK failures before returning failure, so an earlier fixture error cannot conceal later compiler issues. No test removed or ignored.
+
+M4 production UI83dbcf passed all actual sticks/buttons/touchpad/sensitivity/wireless/keyboard actions (52.104s); artifact13977089573, job131441742613. XCTest PNGs show a rotated/cropped composition despite correct1376x1032 AX window geometry and correct physical touch callbacks. Original images retained. Add direct UIKit window pixel captures to the test-only fixture plus preserved Simulator container images, required outside modal settings, to distinguish compositor capture metadata from actual control layout. No shipping runtime capture/timer added. Exact next-source UI validation still required; physical Duo/M4 remains distinct.
+
+Duo83 actualUI artifacts13979127757/job131441742617 show: (1)local compact gamepad pointer drag produced zero callbacks, (2)tabletop parent accessibilityIdentifier propagated over every child, replacing both native gamepad/touchpad IDs. Remove parent IDs from tabletop/video containers; tests assert video/controller geometry through leaf elements. Use exact unique IDs across AX types because the runtime explicitly reports legacy TextView versus modern Other for UIKeyInput. Replace the separately offset gamepad pointer representable with one native ControllerCanvasView that hosts the existing PadView/LinkInputView, positions both subviews in one coordinate space and preserves transparent hit passthrough. No duplicate input/gyro/transport model; resize cancels held pointer gestures, unchanged updates preserve input. Must verify on actual next-source M4/Duo-canvas UI, including40px pointer drag.
+
+Native4e8946 run43294128029/job131447763306 PASSED all checks including USB/gamepad coexistence, actual ordinary guest helper launch, Swift6 helper, bundle signatures, production phone/simulator SDK, macOSclone/GPT, lifecycle/sanitizers and full iOS Release app compilation. No IPA generated. New UIKit composition and test pixel capture changes still require exact-source gate.
