+Loading follow-up, 2026-11-13 (implementation; IPA gate closed)
+
+Latest supplied fd3681d/0.3.6 Duo log contains TWO sessions: 4 CPUs/8GB each;
+long session cache off, shorter session cache on, per-access counters off in both.
+They are not an A/B experiment. The long session recycled 26 JIT segments without
+a full reset, remained thermal category0 in capture, and one PSO build took
+2772.46ms. A bounded capture used ~3.13 process CPU equivalents. Presentation
+counts are not Roblox FPS. Two memory warnings are observable across sessions.
+Older M4 cache-on snapshots reached98%+ kernel LUT hits, but the existing cloud
+microbenchmark shows cache-first overhead on ordinary TLB hits. No physical
+speedup, watt reduction or globally optimal CPU count is established.
+
+Implemented:
+- TLB-first secondary kernel LUT option, same permission/invalidation ownership;
+  no extra hot-hit instructions. Shared production emitter used in both orders.
+- Adjacent virtio block descriptors coalesce into direct guest-buffer transfers;
+  no staging copies; status excluded, RAM spans checked, fences unchanged.
+- Moderate memory warnings retain persistent PSO lookup and flush bounded pending
+  PSOs before discarding loaded handles. Critical/low-headroom fallback retained.
+  Save deadline starts at first pending PSO rather than sliding on every compile.
+- Existing optional renderer metrics now include archive hits/compiles/pending.
+- Removed app Runner UI, guest downloader/launcher, host command queue/long-polls,
+  CPU-background/GPU gating, and redundant Instant Resume foreground hook.
+  One stateless legacy stop response retires old companion-owned child safely;
+  subsequent old requests receive410 until the sharing companion is updated.
+  User-installed runners/repositories/credentials are not deleted.
+- Automatic scheduling/event waits replace retired UI experiments. Old values
+  backed up once; expert henge-env overrides remain authoritative. Duplicated
+  physical mouse toggle removed; meaningful settings retain explanations.
+
+Verification: Linux ASan/UBSan RAM/fastmem/disk/descriptor and4096 raced block
+completions pass. ARM64 Unicorn2088+ cases pass; native macOS/Metal/Swift/lifecycle/ASan checks passed in run43389387394,
+job131765399602 through native stages (full iOS build still running at checkpoint).
+Paired7-round current-engine benchmark, flat: warmed cache-on/off ratios
+0.996/1.005/1.007 (single/two-window/user) vs old1.368/1.267/1.384;
+collision-heavy ratio0.036 (~28x faster than cache off). Split-layout collision
+ratio0.034; ordinary-hit ratios0.936/0.969/0.882 reflect host drift/layout,
+not a claimed physical speedup. Choose TLB-first default for the existing cache.
+Fresh preferences enable it; saved off choices remain off. Explicit M4 Automatic
+selects this cache and disables periodic diagnostics. Full final-source build
+and release gate must still pass before packaging.
+Do not publish an IPA until those actual checks and final gate pass.
+
+Safety decisions: persistent archive hints select candidate files; Metal itself validates the complete descriptor. They are not proof of exact PSO identity, so no unsafe direct pipeline-state reuse is added from those partial keys. Guest-visible CPUs remain static and user selectable; OS scheduling is not physical core pinning. No guest translation persistence across app/JIT launches is claimed.
