+size. Archive files are disposable OS-build/GPU keyed, lazy, capped128MiB/16files,
+excluded from backups, pressure-released; one active-only debounce timer replaces
+a timer per compile. Fresh-process archive reload/corruption/fragmentless tests
+added to real Metal lifecycle fixture. Existing fixed cursor preferences win;
+Auto uses the guest panel density via cached settings, including Link mirrors.
+
+First native checkpoint compiled all engine objects. Full-flush fixture now
+explicitly selects segment1; ring concurrency has its own four-vCPU fixture.
+Fixed extracted-C dependencies and the GPU delete command's 12-byte header.
+Portable real chain/index/allocator publication tests pass. All failures remain
+release-blocking until the next complete native/graphics/app run is green.
+
+PR143 adaptation: Safari b3a8 allocations use guest pages only on Apple9-capable
+Metal devices after both canonical plane views pass runtime bounds/format probes.
+Other formats retain IOSurface. Allocation backing stays fixed and exact page/layout
+identity follows live texture ownership. This avoids the proposed lazy promotion
+mixing already-encoded guest and host views. Reference escape: HV_PVG_PLANAR_COPY=1.
+Native fixture checks the decision and GPU writes into actual shared-buffer bytes;
+Apple Paravirtual CI may exercise only the reference branch, explicitly reported.
+
+Archive fallback now clears descriptor binaryArchives before fragmentless compilation
+and after cache misses; reused descriptors cannot poison the normal compiler path.
+The four-vCPU stress fixture uses a working set beyond ideal deduplicated cache
+capacity rather than relying on concurrent chunk wastage to cause eviction.
+
+Latest review decisions (main e98920c; PR heads fixed in wrapper manifest):
+- PR134 keeps default TLB size14. Its configurable layout and profiling-only
+  additions do not establish a desktop speedup. This fork retains size14 and
+  its existing opt-in counters instead of mixing differently sized native/glue
+  objects or changing the MMU layout without a device comparison.
+- PR157's EL0 window is explicitly an off-by-default prototype. Its signal
+  handler takes the window spin lock and calls vm_remap/mprotect; remote drops
+  and code-page protection take that same lock. It would also add a second
+  translation cache to every ASID/range/PAN/code invalidation path and compete
+  with our JIT fault guards. No async-signal/reentrancy validation is supplied
+  for this fork, so the proven tagged-TLB/read-span path remains authoritative.
+  Shared-region keeping depends on dropping every user entry on ASID invalidation;
+  it cannot be copied independently of the prototype's stash/invalidation changes.
+  Its parent table-attribute checks are present; that is not the rejection reason.
+- PR135/154 are single-display live-mode/built-in-panel protocol changes. They
+  replace display_pa/swaps whereas this fork owns two independently restored
+  ports, Link monitor routing and USB touchscreen display UUID association.
+  Built-in reporting deliberately bypasses the driver's external IOMFBUUID path.
+  Preserve the tested two-port/snapshot/UUID implementation; these are not a
+  normal desktop throughput fix. No automatic built-in flag or rotation merge.
+- PR138/139/141 overlap the existing tested audio recovery, grow-only disk
+  expansion and device-aware CPU options. Keep one implementation of each.
+- PR80/81 do not justify raising every vCPU QoS or enabling experimental
+  superblocks on M4/Duo. Supported QoS hints remain distinct from core pinning;
+  normal Retina/60-120Hz settings and four-vCPU Automatic remain unchanged.
+
+Final focused corrections: resource captures use atomic ring extent reads and
+reset publication, always bounded by effective capacity. A successful Metal
+archive insertion is reused for state creation; only rejected/fragmentless paths
+clear attachments before normal compilation, avoiding a second compiler pass.
+
+Native checkpoint f720a1c: four-vCPU normal/poison/split runs pass with
+331/1542/275 evictions and zero capacity full resets; all architectural register
+counters correct. Original JIT reference tests pass36-37evictions/25exit repairs,
+11programs with zero failures, including superblocks/split and sanitizers.
+Safari cloud probe reports direct=0 (Apple Paravirtual lacks Apple9); real
+IOSurface fallback and lifetime tests execute. Remaining Metal failure was an
+invalid fixture: rasterization disabled requires a void-return vertex shader.
+Added that real shader; fragmentless archive bypass remains asserted.
+
+Second Metal checkpoint: legal fragmentless pipeline and six complete lifecycle
+cycles pass in the ordinary native test. Repeated fresh-process/sanitizer tests
+exposed archive-backed state creation failure after a successful archive add.
+Now retry that valid descriptor with no archives, clear successful-call errors,
+and retain real compilation errors on nil results. Required fresh-process hit
+assertions remain; no archive test or unsupported format check is skipped.
+
+Early failure artifact confirms ordinary compilation now succeeds after an
+archive function-hash miss; hit assertions correctly remain failing. New archive
+adds exclude older descriptor archives and retain the actual destination through
+save rotation, making newly serialized pipelines self-contained. The test fixture
+now loads identical precompiled metallib bytes across processes instead of
+regenerating runtime source library identities; this matches the production path.
+No cache-hit requirement is weakened and the real shader states still execute
+through the production cache/lifecycle code.
+
+Root cause established independently of Henge (run43339413343, artifact13998139090,
+SHA2568ea75284cb3e0aa31a8abdbf94dc3db355883ef1cc6618baea28f21eeca6dbe0):
+public Metal API render-only save reopens with a hit in a new process; adding
+compute to that same file loses the render af function on reload. Ordinary
+compilation succeeds. No blanket unsupported-GPU exemption is needed.
+
+Repair: one manager, one total128MiB/16file budget and one debounce timer, with
+separate render/compute/tile writers and loaded-file lists. Schema2 discards old
+mixed files. Writers are lazy, release on pressure/stop and preserve the exact
+container through save rotation. Native fresh-process tests require BOTH render
+and compute hits from separate files. The unused mixed reference case records
+its actual supported/unsupported result and verifies normal compilation on a miss;
+it does not excuse a failure in either production container.
+
+Additional fixture coverage now uses the real guest function-record contract:
+each exact metallib contains one entrypoint (the production loader explicitly
+rejects multi-entrypoint function records). Independent public API controls keep
+the multi-entrypoint library to retain evidence of its stage/function collision.
+The production fixture requires multiple distinct render and compute PSOs to
+reload cold, with distinct single-function library bytes and no relaxed hit checks.
+Settings descriptions now distinguish JIT translations from saved shaders and
+CPU-only background grants from the additional GPU entitlement requirement.
+
+Final archive repair uses one pipeline per native archive because multi-compute
+cold tests also lost earlier functions. Schema3 indexes SHA256 function/data and
+public pipeline-state hints; Metal still validates every full descriptor on hit.
+At most4 opaque variants per hint,16 loaded handles,64 pending writes and2048
+files/128MiB total. Files open lazily; eviction permits new shaders instead of
+permanently stopping admission. One active-only timer; pressure releases owners.
+Cold tests retain all four distinct PSO hit assertions and oversized/corrupt cache
+rejection. This replaces the unsuccessful multi-pipeline writer, not a new cache
+alongside it. Actual native results remain required before release.
+
+Storage repair checkpoint: persistent Finish volume expansion UI now inspects the
+actual GPT, including disks expanded by older builds. A strict offline preparation
+can move a single trailing APFS Recovery container onto a private clone only after
+validating both GPTs, nonoverlap, partition type and NX superblock checksum. Copies
+are byte-verified; UUIDs and original image remain preserved. macOS diskutil owns
+APFS data-volume growth. Linux ASan/UBSan production tests cover inspection, both
+GPT CRCs, aligned nonoverlapping relocation, payload preservation, bad NX/type
+rejection and idempotence. Real guest Recovery boot/volume growth remains a device
+validation requirement. Metal cache cold-compute reload still fails the strict
+cloud gate; collecting key/miss errors and independent four-PSO file probes.
+
+Concrete cloud-adapter exception (run43347567023): independent public Metal API
+with four separate files reproduces a cold ak missing-function error, even with
+immediate serialization. Henge's stable key matches the indexed file. This is
+not a delayed-save/key mismatch. The independent control now uses exact separate
+single-entrypoint binaries, tests all four PSOs, executes both kernels and checks
+their numeric outputs. Only the Paravirtual missing-function result with verified
+ordinary fallback may declare that adapter's cold compute persistence unavailable.
+Other device errors remain fatal. Production tests still require cold render and
+all warm cache hits, execute both compute states, exercise fallback/pressure/stop,
+and require cold compute hits on physical GPUs. No product fast path is disabled.
+Real M4/Duo cold compute persistence is a hardware-only performance validation.
+
+Follow-up run43348358520: executing both compute kernels before saving made ALL
+four production PSOs reload with real cold hits in all cycles and fresh processes.
+Their numeric outputs were verified on the GPU. The production fixture now models
+real pipeline use; ALL FOUR cold-hit assertions are retained unconditionally
+(no capability/environment exception). Independent API controls still reproduce
+Paravirtual missing-function behavior for compute and occasionally the second
+render format, despite successful save; every such case must execute its ordinary
+fallback correctly. This adapter-specific public-API observation does not relax
+the actual production cache hit tests. Physical latency gains remain unmeasured.
+Added a real disposable raw-image/APFS integration test: vendor-created filesystems,
+Recovery relocation, diskutil root-container growth and mounted payload/filesystem
+verification, with strict image-to-device ownership. This tests actual APFS data
+without pretending to boot a complete Recovery OS.
