+# Upstream review, 12 November 2026
+
+Reviewed current main 1812892e129c149cf68cfa0f5e26de7f92e94fba and inventoried all 69 PRs (open/closed). Main's 44 commits since the integrated 8048e4a base affect direct Mac Apps / translation-layer loading, not the VM core, devices or host. They are not evidence of a macOS-desktop or Roblox FPS gain. Full inventory is adjacent; no blanket merge or hardware measurement is claimed.
+
+| PR | Decision / concrete integration concern |
+| --- | --- |
+| 32 | Implement new entitlement-free emulated USB touchscreen for supported macOS 27.2+ guests. Must move its port from 3 to 4, preserve gamepad port 3, reconcile snapshots and guest-helper packaging. Pending. |
+| 103 | Reuse the horizontal active reserved-region API for controller posture; do not import a second SessionView layout engine. Manual override when no region is reported. Actual SDK/UI validation pending. |
+| 123 | Useful windowed iPad absolute-pointer path; also claims USB port 3. Requires port reconciliation and pointer-lock/relative-event deduplication. Not imported blindly. |
+| 72 | Useful separately configurable keyboard shortcut interception and focus-loss release; reconcile current StickyKeys and input owners before adoption. |
+| 130 | Multi-device JIT pairing candidate validation may improve attach reliability, not steady FPS. Needs ordered candidate/cancellation tests. |
+| 128 | Forward genuine debugger faults rather than treating every stop as a JIT BRK. Valuable stability change; test alongside existing trap guard/detachment. |
+| 126 | OpenGL renderer-name metadata could avoid software fallback in affected apps. Whole-RAM scan budget is process-static; must become per-VM before adoption. Its F20 wake heuristic misclassifies an unchanged damage-driven desktop as asleep, so reject that heuristic. No evidence this accelerates Roblox's Metal path. |
+| 121 | Required companion if adopting newer Chromium high-address holds. Current fork has no corresponding reservation path, so it cannot fix current VM RAM/FPS. |
+| 117 | Selected late Metal store-action correctness fix already integrated and tested. Large LLVM/iOS17 renderer replacement would conflict with retained iOS27 native renderer. |
+| 108 / 109 / 106 | Duo screen fit / scaled pointer-click equivalents already integrated; do not duplicate. |
+| 112 | Keep existing atomic GPU timing. PR's unsynchronised last-completion state and duplicate callbacks are inferior. |
+| 92 | Fork already hashes all surface bytes and validates full uploads; do not describe it as sampled hashing or add a second scanner. |
+| 98 | Preserve fractional/coalesced hardware scrolling; shared touchpad sensitivities improve the existing gesture path without another timer. |
+| 78 / 80 / 81 | Configurable JIT size and experimental superblocks already exist. Aggressive QoS/more code is not proven cooler or faster under Low Power Mode. Retain safe defaults. |
+| 74 / 76 / 77 | DAV caching/locks/restart are potentially useful for shared files. Restart patch's volatile globals lack safe in-flight draining; not safe to merge unchanged. |
+| 79 / 82 / 87 / 90 / 93 | Input/geometry overlap with current three-finger menu, native touch, saved display config and pointer scaling. Preserve one authoritative path and settings. |
+| 83 / 84 / 91 / 100 | Emulated Bluetooth/camera/microphone are separate feature work, not physical USB passthrough or a VM speed fix. |
+| 114 / 115 / 127 / 129 | JIS keyboard / external downloads / new-disk sizing / direct-app bundle compatibility are scoped usability fixes, not measured macOS guest performance improvements. |
+
+Existing cooling diagnosis remains: latest supplied slow-FPS logs used the older 0.3.3 binary with six guest CPUs, 10GB RAM, experimental grouped/superblock paths and detailed counters under Low Power Mode. Normal thermal state does not imply spare CPU scheduling capacity; host presentation counts are not game FPS. Preserve controlled four-vCPU/eight-GB defaults, Retina quality, and disabled expensive release diagnostics. Do not promise a frame-rate improvement from these controller changes.
